⚠️ Problem Faced

Video generation can encounter problems if the output cannot be encoded correctly or if the video-processing tools are unavailable. The generated animation may also contain unnatural movements even when the output file is created.

✅ Resolution
Reviewed the FFmpeg-related processing steps.
Checked the output file and its playback.
Examined the generated frames to identify visual inconsistencies.
Kept input processing and output generation as separate troubleshooting stages.
🖼️ Project Picture

Generated output video alongside the original driving video for comparison.

💡 Learning

I learned that generating a video file is not enough to establish good results. Both technical output quality and the naturalness of the animation need to be checked.
